findings.body:
**A Ctrl-C during a batch fetch doesn't stop the batch.** `fetchTarget` wraps the killed git's error in a new `Error` with no `signal`. The batch then skips that session and lands the rest.

Under the lock, `withMergeLock` installs a no-op listener for SIGINT (`merge-gate.service.ts` L1243-1244). Its JSDoc says a terminal Ctrl-C kills only the child git, and that the child's failure then unwinds the stack. That failure is the only signal of the interrupt. `fetchTarget`'s catch drops it ([land.service.ts#L624-L629](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/3b16873c74e6026fb76a4f2b6911fb2f2ce1ece4/src/core/land.service.ts#L624-L629)):

```ts
} catch (error) {
  throw new Error(
    `Fetching ${fetched} from ${sanitizeReason(originUrl)} failed. Nothing was landed.\n` +
      failureSummary(error),
  );
}
```

The catch has no `rethrowIfKilled`, unlike its siblings `descendsFrom` and `steerOverlappingSessions`. `rethrowIfKilled` checks only the error's own `signal`, so these checks can never fire for a killed fetch:

- **The ordering fetch in `inMergeOrder`** ([L151-L162](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/3b16873c74e6026fb76a4f2b6911fb2f2ce1ece4/src/core/land-batch.service.ts#L151-L162)). The `instanceof GateInterruptedError` / `rethrowIfKilled` guard is dead code. The interrupt is swallowed, the order falls back to the order the sessions were named in, and every session lands. The full audit then runs, about 330 s. Commit 45b87cb says this case is "rethrown, not swallowed".
- **Each land's own fetch** (`landUnderLock`, then the loop catch at [L81-L86](https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/3b16873c74e6026fb76a4f2b6911fb2f2ce1ece4/src/core/land-batch.service.ts#L81-L86), then `refusalOf` at L118-122). The interrupt becomes an ordinary refusal and the loop moves on to the next session. One Ctrl-C skips one session, and the run exits 1 instead of 130.

The catch itself is pre-existing. On the single-land path the wrapped error still ended the run. The new catch-and-continue loop is what turns an interrupt into "skip this session and keep landing".

**Fix:** add `rethrowIfKilled(error);` as the first statement of `fetchTarget`'s catch, as `descendsFrom` does. Also add a land-batch test that kills a fetch with SIGINT and asserts that no later session lands and the audit doesn't run. `src/core/land-batch.test.ts` has no interrupt test today.
